  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_031 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) at 0.678 acc. RNA-only with scvi_n200+avgpool is 0.650, so image adds ~2.8 pts only with weighted fusion. However, image-only with resnet50 was very weak (0.208), raising the question of whether the image modality's contribution is bottlenecked by encoder capacity. Uncertainty: We have only tested resnet50 as the image encoder; it is unclear whether a stronger pretrained encoder (imagenet_vit_l) would meaningfully improve the image signal and thus the multimodal result. This experiment (config_037) changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other parameters at their best-known values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted), giving a clean single-variable comparison to config_031. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly tests whether the image modality can contribute more signal, which determines whether further multimodal experiments should invest in image quality or whether we should focus remaining budget on RNA-side improvements."
}

